Appendix: Training Quiz – Questions & Answers (Including Multiple Choice)

HEAT Model – Knowledge Check

1. What does the “H” in the HEAT model stand for?

A. Help

B. Hear

C. Handle

D. Hold
✅ Correct answer: B. Hear (Hear them out)



2. Which of the following best demonstrates empathy in a conversation?

A. “That’s not a big deal.”

B. “You’ll have to call another job.”

C. “I understand why you’re feeling frustrated.”

D. “There’s nothing I can do.”
✅ Correct answer: C. “I understand why you’re feeling frustrated.”



3. What is the purpose of the “A” (Apologise) in the HEAT model?

A. To accept full responsibility

B. To calm the caller

C. To acknowledge the impact of the situation

D. To end the call
✅ Correct answer: C. To acknowledge the impact of the situation



4. Which statement is an appropriate apology in a heated conversation?

A. “I’m sorry you feel that way.”

B. “This isn’t my fault.”

C. “I’m sorry this situation has caused you frustration.”

D. “You should have handled this earlier.”
✅ Correct answer: C. “I’m sorry this situation has caused you frustration.”



5. What does “Take Action” involve in the HEAT model?

A. Ending the call quickly

B. Explaining next steps and solutions

C. Agreeing with the complaint

D. Escalating every issue
✅ Correct answer: B. Explaining next steps and solutions



6. Which of the following is not recommended when managing a heated conversation?

A. Showing empathy

B. Listening actively

C. Telling the caller to calm down

D. Explaining available options
✅ Correct answer: C. Telling the caller to calm down



7. Why is empathy critical in heated conversations?

A. It shortens the call

B. It proves the caller is right

C. It reduces tension and builds trust

D. It avoids policy requirements
✅ Correct answer: C. It reduces tension and builds trust



8. What is the overall goal of using the HEAT model?

A. To prove the customer is wrong

B. To end calls faster

C. To maintain professionalism and reach positive outcomes

D. To avoid difficult conversations
✅ Correct answer: C. To maintain professionalism and reach positive outcomes





